Subject: Guard OnWorkerTaskCompleted and clear Member fields on Shutdown

Follow-up cleanup to AnimationFrameTimingMonitor::Shutdown():
- Add an enabled_ guard to OnWorkerTaskCompleted() for consistency with
  OnMainThreadTaskCompleted() so worker tasks completing after
  Shutdown() are ignored.
- Clear current_frame_timing_info_, current_scripts_,
  congestion_scripts_, and task_attributed_window_ in Shutdown() so GC
  can reclaim referenced objects sooner.

Bug: 566506819
Change-Id: I65ea95b83008425a7df8ec49cd94d5c76a6a6964
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8498065
Reviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal <nrosenthal@google.com>
Commit-Queue: Michal Mocny <mmocny@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1711207}

Electron adaptation notes (43-x-y):
This branch's AnimationFrameTimingMonitor has no worker-thread support (no OnWorkerTaskCompleted(), congestion_scripts_ or task_attributed_window_), so only the Shutdown() change applies here: it now clears current_frame_timing_info_ and current_scripts_ as upstream does. The OnWorkerTaskCompleted() guard has no counterpart on this branch.

